{"name":"Shrimp Cocktail","hex":"#f4a461","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shrimp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many swimming, often edible, crustaceans, chiefly of the infraorder Caridea or the suborder Dendrobranchiata, with slender legs, long whiskers and a long abdomen.","The flesh of such crustaceans."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for shrimp.","To contract; to shrink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrimp"},{"term":"cocktail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixed alcoholic beverage.","A mixture of other substances or things."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ostentatiously lacking in manners."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocktail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prawn cocktail","blocks":[{"text":"Prawn cocktail, also known as shrimp cocktail, is a seafood dish consisting of shelled, cooked prawns in a Marie Rose sauce or cocktail sauce, served in a glass. It was the most popular hors d'œuvre in Great Britain, as well as in the United States, from the 1960s to the late 1980s. According to the English food writer Nigel Slater, the prawn cocktail \"has spent most of see-sawing from the height of fashion to the laughably passé\" and is now often served with a degree of irony."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Cocktail_1_bg_060702.jpg/330px-Cocktail_1_bg_060702.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prawn_cocktail","wikidata":"Q3776982"},{"title":"Shrimp","blocks":[{"text":"A shrimp is a common name typically used for crustaceans with an elongated body and a primarily swimming mode of locomotion. The name usually refers to decapods belonging to the Caridea or Dendrobranchiata, although some crustaceans outside this order are also referred to as \"shrimp\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg/330px-Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp","wikidata":"Q1517781"},{"title":"Cocktail","blocks":[{"text":"A cocktail is a mixed drink, usually alcoholic. Most commonly, a cocktail is a combination of one or more spirits mixed with other ingredients, such as juices, flavored syrups, tonic water, shrubs, and bitters. Cocktails vary widely across regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg/330px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocktail","wikidata":"Q134768"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/American-style_Shrimp_Cocktail%2C_September_2014.jpg/500px-American-style_Shrimp_Cocktail%2C_September_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/American-style_Shrimp_Cocktail%2C_September_2014.jpg/500px-American-style_Shrimp_Cocktail%2C_September_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An American-style shrimp cocktail made with store-bought cocktail sauce and garnished with endive and dill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmerican-style_Shrimp_Cocktail%2C_September_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Prawn_cocktail.jpg/500px-Prawn_cocktail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Prawn_cocktail.jpg/1280px-Prawn_cocktail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Prawn_cocktail.jpg/500px-Prawn_cocktail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont